                <pb facs="0721" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2638: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-29T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 29,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 29—11:20
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>29. Referring to Legation’s telegram January 27, 5 p.m. The Japanese Minister
                    proposes that the four Legations concerned instruct the four banks concerned to
                    make certain advances to the Chinese Government to enable it to tide over the
                    Chinese New Year <pb facs="0722" n="624" xml:id="pg624"/> settlement day, such
                    advances to be deducted 5,000,000 pounds loan when arranged. Please telegraph
                    instructions without delay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
